        "title": "Ocean-Atmosphere Coupling",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The ocean and atmosphere are coupled systems — they exchange heat, moisture,\nand momentum continuously. The ocean stores 90%+ of excess planetary heat and\nmoderates climate over decadal timescales. Understanding ENSO, thermohaline\ncirculation, and teleconnections is prerequisite to understanding regional\nclimate variability, drought cycles, and the mechanisms by which climate change\npropagates spatially."
    },
